    "summary": "Built the deterministic 1v1 duel as pure integer code. packages/content/src/moves holds the input bits, zod schemas and validators (the move timing reuses moveTimingSchema), the Duelist moveset (jab, heavy mid, low sweep and throw take their timing objects from baselineFrameBudgets; launcher, anti-air, advancing thrust and counter slash are the worker's choice), the \u00a77 rules, the arena, MOVESET_VERSION 'duelist-1' and the input-log schema. packages/simulation/src/duel holds the state, stepDuel (inputs, then detection against the start-of-frame state, then same-frame interactions, then simultaneous apply, then movement, then stamina and result), boxes, snapshotDuel/restoreDuel, replayDuel/traceDuel/sliceDuelInputLog and createDuelInputLog. Subpath exports @pirate-sea-race/simulation/duel and @pirate-sea-race/content/moves follow the existing pattern, and each package has a postbuild that imports its subpath from dist/ without the source condition (it exits 1 when the source condition sends it to src/). docs/duel.md is written. Tests: 47 rule tests (round, timeout, overtime, double KO, a KO on the final frame, simultaneous hits, movement, walls, pushboxes, guard levels, throws with escape window, clash and strike priority, stamina costs, regeneration and guard break, combo scaling and cap, the 4-frame buffer, heavy mid -12 punished by a jab in the corner at max range and midscreen), 10 determinism, rollback, version and symmetry tests (frame-by-frame mirror with slots swapped; a one-sub-pixel wall asymmetry was confirmed to fail it), and 40 content validator tests. Checks run in this worktree after npm ci: npm run typecheck (exit 0), npm run test:unit (183 passed), npm run test:integration (14 passed), npm run build (exit 0; both postbuild self-checks and the build smoke test passed). No commits were made; only owned paths changed.",
